// The SAPIC type tag on a variable that only a conditional mentions.
//
// A SAPIC condition is parsed by `standardFormula sapicvar sapicnodevar`
// (Theory/Text/Parser/Sapic.hs:252-255, one instantiation of
// Theory/Text/Parser/Formula.hs:108-109#standardFormula), so its variables
// are `SapicLVar`s: `sapicvar` reads an optional `:type` and leaves the tag
// `Nothing` otherwise (Theory/Text/Parser/Token.hs:506-510#sapicvar), while
// `sapicnodevar` stamps `Just "node"`
// (Theory/Text/Parser/Token.hs:522-525#sapicnodevar,
// Theory/Sapic/Term.hs:99-100#defaultSapicNodeType).
//
// The tag reaches the printed theory.  A process definition written without
// formals takes its formals from `S.toList (varsProc pr) \\ accBindings pr`
// (Sapic/Typing.hs:219#pvars); `varsProc = foldMap Data.Set.singleton`
// (Theory/Sapic/Process.hs:361-362#varsProc) over the derived `Foldable`
// reaches the condition's free variables, and `-m=spthytyped` prints them
// with `map show`
// (TheoryObject.hs:791-799#prettyTranslationElement), where
// `show (SapicLVar v (Just t)) = show v ++ ":" ++ t`
// (Theory/Sapic/Term.hs:108-110).  Four of the five `let` lines below carry a
// tag, so this row is what pins the tag all the way to the printed bytes.
//
// The tagging is POSITIONAL, and row `V` is the measurement of that:
// `blatom` writes `nodevarTerm = lit . Var <$> nodep` for `last`'s argument,
// an action's timepoint and both operands of `<`
// (Theory/Text/Parser/Formula.hs:44-57#blatom), while a predicate atom takes
// `fact (vlit (try varp <|> nodep))`, where `sapicvar` wins for every
// spelling — so `#p` inside `Pred` stays untagged and only `S`, `T` and `U`
// carry `:node`.
//
// Flags: `-m=spthytyped`, the one mode that prints a process definition's
// formals.  No corpus theory is loaded in that mode, and no corpus condition
// mentions a timepoint, a `last`, a `<` or a `:type`, so this row is the only
// check on the tag.
//
// Compared slice: the `theory … end` echo, which in this mode carries the
// five `let` declarations and the `process:` block.

theory SapicCondTypeTag
begin

predicates: Eq(a, b) <=> a = b, Pred(a, b) <=> a = a

let P = if Eq(x:foo, 'a') then out('yes') else out('no')
let S = if #k < #l then out('yes') else out('no')
let T = if last(#m) then out('yes') else out('no')
let U = if Ev(x)@#n then out('yes') else out('no')
let V = if Pred(#p, y) then out('yes') else out('no')

process:
  out('done')

end
